    {
      "short": "Index cost",
      "chapter": "tradeoff",
      "title": "Indexes aren't free",
      "body": [
        "Indexes cost write performance (every insert updates the index too — ~8% in our sim) and storage. Index what you query, not everything.",
        "Watch query plans, not just CPU — a healthy CPU chart can hide a pathological query shape."
      ],
      "changes": [
        "+ B-tree index on the lookup key",
        "~ Write cost: +8%",
        "~ Query latency: 5000ms → 5ms"
      ],
